ve oil 1/2 a teaspoon  of cumin and half a teaspoon of smoked  paprika in a small bowl combine lime  juice olive oil cumin and smoked paprika  set aside in a large bowl add black  beans sweet potato red onion and  coriander combine well toss in the  dressing and season with salt and pepper  mix until evenly coated spoon generous  amount of black beans and sweet potato  mixture onto lettuce leaves so simple  and yummy if you're a vegan and you  enjoy Asian flavors then make this spicy  tofu mushroom lettuce wraps for the  filling you need one packet of firm tofu  drained and cut into small cubes 1 cup  of button mushroom chopped 1/2 a medium  red bell pepper diced into cubes a  handful of fresh coriander finely sliced  quarter cup of cashew nuts crushed 2  small red chili this seeded and finely  sliced and 1/2 a tbsp of sesame oil to  make the dressing you'll need juice from  one line 2 tablespoons of soy sauce and  1 tbsp of water in a small bowl combine  lime juice soy sauce and water set aside  heat sesame oil over medium-high heat  add mushroom and cook for 2 to 3 minutes  until slightly tender add tofu and sear  until lightly Brown for another 2 to 3  minutes on each side  toss in red bell pepper chili and cashew  nuts cook very quickly for another 1  minute and stir in the soya sauce  mixture continue cooking for another 2  to 3 minutes until sauce has reduced  slightly remove from heat and allow it  to cool down to serve spoon generous  amount of tofu mixture onto lettuce  leaves and sprinkle with coriander tofu  is a great source of protein for vegans  and  drum is packed with vitamin D and the  hint of chilli adds a nice twist to the  dish next is another Asian flavored  lettuce wrap with my all-time favorite  protein smoked salmon for the filling  you'll need 100 gram of smoked salmon  sliced 1/2 a cup of carrots shredded 1/2  a cup of cucumber shredded and half a  cup of cherry tomatoes haft to make the  dressing you'll need juice from one line  half a tab